     <h1 class="title" title="Yelagiri Hill Station">Yelagiri</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/yelagiri-hill-station.jpg" title="Yelagiri hill station" alt="Yelagiri hill station, hill stations in india, South india hill stations, Yelagiri" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Tamil Nadu<br />
<b>Area:</b> 6sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Tranquil lake<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 920m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 26&#176;C to 31&#176;C, Winter 14&#176;C to 20&#176;C.<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b> November and February</p>
<p><b>Yelagiri Hill</b> is one of the most popular <b>hill stations in Tamil Nadu</b>. Located in the center of four mountains, known as a healthy climate prevails throughout the year. people living in tribal villages in these hills. If you are traveling winding Ghat road with 14 switchbacks you reach <b>Yelagiri hills</b>. Hairpin bends overlooking the balcony with stunning views of the mountains and the surrounding area.</p>





